    "https://lagrangecollege.applicantstack.com/x/detail/a2pbzv144y95": {
      "title": "Faculty Appointment",
      "description": "Faculty Appointment - Education - LaGrange College Job Openings >> Faculty Appointment - Education Faculty Appointment - Education Summary Title: Faculty Appointment - Education ID: 1446 Department: Education Description LaGrange College seeks to fill a tenure-track teaching appointment  at the assistant or associate professor level effective August 1, 2026.  The successful candidate must have a Doctorate in Education in curriculum, pedagogy, teacher leadership or related area; and documented accomplishments in educational research, preferably related to PK-12 teaching.  Experience teaching in P-12 classrooms or experience as an instructional and/or teacher leader is helpful but not required The faculty member will be  a respected teacher leader who will  primarily teach courses at the  EdD program level, although there may be requirements to teach in other programs offered (B.A, M.Ed., and Ed.S.) as needed and as appropriate to their field(s) of specialization. The Master of Education (M.Ed.), Education Specialist (Ed.S.) and Educational Doctorate (Ed.D.)  in Curriculum and Instruction programs help classroom teachers improve their planning, instructional and assessment skills. LaGrange College Mission Statement We challenge the minds and inspire the souls of our students, preparing them to become successful, responsible citizens who pursue lives of integrity, service, and lifelong learning. LaGrange College Value Statement As an Institution, we value: The inherent worth of every human being Pursuit of lifelong learning and development Integrity and moral courage Spiritual growth Service to our community and to our world Interested candidates should visit https://lagrangecollege.applicantstack.com/x/openings to apply for the position and to view other positions available at the college. Required documents include: A letter of interest describing the alignment of the candidate’s qualifications with the position requirements Current curriculum vitae A statement of teaching philosophy that also addresses ways in which the candidate creates and sustains a culture of belonging, fairness and appreciation for different perspectives in the classroom Graduate and undergraduate transcripts (unofficial copies are fine at this point) Contact information (only) for three professional references The review of applications will begin on January 15 and continue until the position is filled. The successful candidate will be required to undergo a background check as a prerequisite for the position. Any questions about the position should be addressed to officeoftheVPAA@lagrange.edu . LaGrange College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, gender, sex, age, national origin, disability, veteran status or any other legally protected status. Apply Now Copyright 2026 LaGrange College. All rights reserved. Powered by ApplicantStack™ Hiring Software Privacy Policy | Terms of Use"
    },
    "https://lagrangecollege.applicantstack.com/x/detail/a2pbzv1sdmw2": {
      "title": "Department Chair, Nursing",
      "description": "Department Chair, Nursing - LaGrange College Job Openings >> Department Chair, Nursing Department Chair, Nursing Summary Title: Department Chair, Nursing ID: 1477 Department: Nursing Description LaGrange College announces an opening for the Chair’s position in the Department of Nursing. Candidates whose credentials include significant experience are encouraged to apply. This is a full-time, tenure-track position (rank open) with a start date of 1st August 2027 and will involve teaching 18 credit hours per fiscal year in addition to the responsibilities of Chair. Candidates should be willing to demonstrate inter-professional collaboration as a member of the Chairs Council meeting with the VPAA and other Department Chairs to discuss issues that affect curricula across the college and within programs. Administrative duties include but are not limited to representing departmental and faculty interests within the college, managing and evaluating faculty and administrative staff, and overseeing physical and financial resources. The Chair and nursing faculty are in periodic discussions of student achievement and challenges during course delivery. The LaGrange College program in Nursing, in its 44th year, is a fast-growing major on campus. The degree program in Nursing offers a traditional BSN program. The LaGrange College nursing program is accredited by the Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing and approved by the Georgia Board of Nursing. Candidates must hold a PhD in Nursing or a DNP and a license in the state of Georgia. Candidates should have knowledge and experience in nursing education regulatory and accreditation requirements General Statement of Duties: Full-time, tenure-track position (rank open), to teach a range of courses leading to the BS degree in Nursing. Potential courses to teach may include but are not limited to: Leadership, Research, Medical-Surgical nursing, Health Assessment and Foundations and On-line degree completion courses. Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Chair the Department of Nursing 2. Teach a total of 18 hours per fiscal year. 3. Supervise student preceptorships. 4. Provide student assistance including academic advising. 5. Attend college functions, including commencement; convocation; and faculty, committee and departmental meetings. 6. Participate in scheduled orientation and registration of new students. 7. Manage course schedules. 8. Assist in the recruitment of students and lead the Admissions Committee of the nursing department. 9. Negotiate contracts related to clinical facility use of students. 10. Provide leadership in ongoing evaluation of Program and Student Outcomes. 11. Maintain documentation on preceptors and clinical adjuncts, including license verification. 12. Conduct yearly faculty evaluations. Minimum Qualifications: 1. Earned DNP or PhD in Nursing. 2. Ability to integrate appropriate technology and software in teaching. 3. Demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching, demonstrated teaching and clinical experience appropriate to the level of appointment, and evidence of scholarly/creative activity. 4. Ability to work effectively with a diverse student body. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: 1. Knowledge of higher education environment and of current student development theory and research. 2. Excellent oral and written communication skills 3. Strong organizational and people leadership skills and the ability to effectively interact with a diverse group of students, staff, faculty, alumni, donors, industry partners, and community. Interested candidates should visit https://lagrangecollege.applicantstack.com/x/openings to apply for the position and to view other positions available at the college. Required documents include: · A letter of interest describing the alignment of the candidate’s qualifications with the position requirements · Current curriculum vitae · A statement of teaching philosophy that also addresses ways in which the candidate creates and sustains a culture of belonging, fairness and appreciation for different         perspectives in the classroom · Graduate and undergraduate transcripts (copies are fine at this point) · Contact information (only) for three professional references The review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. The successful candidate will be required to undergo a background check as a prerequisite for the position. Any questions about the position should be addressed to officeoftheVPAA@lagrange.edu. LaGrange College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, gender, sex, age, national origin, disability, veteran status or any other legally protected status. Apply Now Copyright 2026 LaGrange College. All rights reserved. Powered by ApplicantStack™ Hiring Software Privacy Policy | Terms of Use"
    },
    "https://lagrangecollege.applicantstack.com/x/detail/a2pbzv1b3gly": {
      "title": "Faculty Appointment, Department of Nursing",
      "description": "Faculty Appointment, Department of Nursing - LaGrange College Job Openings >> Faculty Appointment, Department of Nursing Faculty Appointment, Department of Nursing Summary Title: Faculty Appointment, Department of Nursing ID: 1478 Department: Nursing Description Nursing Faculty Position LaGrange College seeks to fill tenure-eligible appointment at the assistant or associate professor level in Nursing beginning August 1, 2027. Field of specialization is open, but preference will be given to candidates with expertise in mental health or medical surgical nursing. An MSN and unencumbered licensure are required for the position; a Doctor of Nursing Practice or Ph.D. in nursing education is required for a tenure-track appointment. The teaching load is 24 credits annually, as appropriate to the successful candidate’s field(s) of specialization in nursing and can include courses that satisfy the college’s general education curriculum, known as Ethos. Candidates should demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching, professional development, and institutional service, as well as an understanding of, and appreciation for, the mission of liberal arts institutions. The nursing program maintains a close relationship with West Georgia Medical Center (Wellstar) and the Children’s Hospital of Atlanta (CHOA). Through both a solid grounding in theory and engagement in the field (via clinical experiences, collaborative undergraduate research, and other opportunities) nursing students receive a thorough, intensive, and experiential education in the discipline. The nursing program recently received an unqualified re-accreditation from ACEN through 2032. Required documents include: A letter of interest describing the alignment of the candidate’s qualifications with the position requirements Current curriculum vitae A teaching philosophy that also addresses ways in which the candidate creates and sustains a culture of belonging, fairness, and appreciation for different perspectives in the classroom Graduate and undergraduate transcripts (copies are fine at this point) Contact information (only) for three professional references Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. The successful candidate will be required to undergo a background check as a prerequisite for the position. Any questions about the position should be addressed to officeoftheVPAA@lagrange.edu. LaGrange College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, gender, sex, age, national origin, disability, veteran status or any other legally protected status. Apply Now Copyright 2026 LaGrange College. All rights reserved. Powered by ApplicantStack™ Hiring Software Privacy Policy | Terms of Use"
    },
    "https://lagrangecollege.applicantstack.com/x/detail/a2pbzv1m96pg": {
      "title": "Faculty Appointment, Art and Design",
      "description": "Faculty Appointment, Art and Design - LaGrange College Job Openings >> Faculty Appointment, Art and Design Faculty Appointment, Art and Design Summary Title: Faculty Appointment, Art and Design ID: 1480 Department: Fine and Performing Arts Description Assistant/Associate Professor of Art and Design (Ceramics/Sculpture) The Department of Art and Design at LaGrange College seeks applicants for a tenure-track faculty position with a primary focus in Ceramics and additional experience in Sculpture. The appointment begins with the 2027-2028 academic year beginning August 2027. Required Qualifications: An MFA in Ceramics or a closely related field; a demonstrated studio practice and exhibition record in ceramics; experience in sculpture sufficient to teach foundational sculpture coursework; and a record of effective teaching at the undergraduate level across a range of ceramics techniques (hand building, wheel-throwing, glaze chemistry, and kiln firing processes). Preferred Qualifications: The ideal candidate will be a strong, energetic leader and an effective communicator and collaborator, invested in growing our ceramics and sculpture offerings, and will help recruit and mentor students. Responsibilities for the position include teaching a range of ceramics courses across skill levels along with Sculpture I (and Sculpture II as needed). The teaching load is 24 credits annually. Responsibilities also include maintaining and developing studio facilities and equipment, including kilns and glaze materials; supervising and ensuring safe operation of the ceramics studio; advising majors and mentoring students toward exhibition opportunities, internships, and professional development. Additional duties may be determined by the successful candidate's experience and abilities. Candidates should demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching, professional development, and institutional service, as well as an understanding of, and appreciation for, the mission of liberal arts institutions. Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience. Interested candidates should visit https://lagrangecollege.applicantstack.com/x/openings to apply for the position and to view other positions available at the college. Required documents include: A letter of interest describing the alignment of the candidate’s qualifications with the position requirements Current curriculum vitae A statement of teaching philosophy that also addresses ways in which the candidate creates and sustains a culture of belonging, fairness and appreciation for different perspectives in the classroom Sample syllabi Work sample portfolio website and/or PDF Student work sample portfolio and/or website link Graduate and undergraduate transcripts (copies are fine at this point) Contact information (only) for three professional references Application Deadline: Review of applications will begin November 16, 2026, and continue until the position is filled.” LaGrange College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, gender, sex, age, national origin, disability, veteran status or any other legally protected status. Apply Now Copyright 2026 LaGrange College. All rights reserved. Powered by ApplicantStack™ Hiring Software Privacy Policy | Terms of Use"
    },
    "https://lagrangecollege.applicantstack.com/x/detail/a2pbzv1m7wb9": {
      "title": "Faculty Appointment, Religious Studies",
      "description": "Faculty Appointment, Religious Studies - LaGrange College Job Openings >> Faculty Appointment, Religious Studies Faculty Appointment, Religious Studies Summary Title: Faculty Appointment, Religious Studies ID: 1479 Department: Humanities & Social Sciences Description LaGrange College seeks to fill a tenure-track position at the assistant professor level in Religious Studies beginning August 1, 2027. The field of specialization is open, but preference will be given to candidates who can teach Christian ethics and broader philosophical approaches to ethics including Bioethics and possibly business ethics and the ethics of AI, as well as candidates prepared to contribute in areas such as American Christianity or world religious traditions. A Ph.D. in religious studies or related field is required, although outstanding ABD candidates will be considered. The successful candidate must have their terminal degree completed prior to the end of their second year in the position. The teaching load is four (4) courses per semester, including introductory courses, upper-level electives in the candidate’s field(s) of specialization, and courses that satisfy the college’s general education curriculum, known as Ethos. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to help shape the future of the major in religion and help create interdisciplinary approaches to critical analyses of American culture and society. The position includes the supervision and mentorship of undergraduate research projects in the field. Candidates should demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching, professional development, and institutional service, as well as an understanding of, and appreciation for, the mission of liberal arts institutions. The religion program maintains a close relationship with the Candler School of Theology at Emory University; students interested in a future ministry career will find a direct and accelerated pathway from LaGrange College to the Candler School of Theology. Through both a solid grounding in theory and engagement in the field (via internships, collaborative undergraduate research, and other opportunities) Religious Studies students receive a thorough, intensive, and experiential education in the discipline. The program’s historic engagement in LaGrange College’s undergraduate research program affords students the opportunity to work directly with faculty on research projects that build their professional skills. The college values its relationship with the United Methodist Church and in particular its commitment to the Wesleyan ideal of service. Interested candidates should visit https://lagrangecollege.applicantstack.com/x/openings to apply for the position and to view other positions available at the college. Required documents include: A letter of interest describing the alignment of the candidate’s qualifications with the position requirements Current curriculum vitae A statement of teaching philosophy that also addresses ways in which the candidate creates and sustains a culture of belonging, fairness and appreciation for different perspectives in the classroom A statement of scholarly interests Graduate and undergraduate transcripts (copies are fine at this point) Contact information (only) for three professional references Review of applications will begin Nov. 9 and will continue until the position is filled. LaGrange College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, gender, sex, age, national origin, disability, veteran status or any other legally protected status. Apply Now Copyright 2026 LaGrange College. All rights reserved. Powered by ApplicantStack™ Hiring Software Privacy Policy | Terms of Use"
    }
